126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (During routine security monitoring, a high-severity alert was generated for suspicious PowerShell activity on the Windows 10 Pro endpoint assigned to Amin. The alert was triggered by a custom Wazuh detection rule designed to identify potentially malicious PowerShell execution.)
/E (During routine security monitoring, a high-severity alert was generated for suspicious PowerShell activity on the Windows 10 Pro endpoint assigned to Amin. The alert was triggered by a custom Wazuh detection rule designed to identify potentially malicious PowerShell execution.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (Initial analysis confirmed that the recorded event matched the expected behavior defined by the custom detection rule. The activity suggested that an attacker, after obtaining access to the endpoint, executed PowerShell with the apparent objective  of preparing the system for subsequent malicious actions while minimizing traces of execution.)
/E (Initial analysis confirmed that the recorded event matched the expected behavior defined by the custom detection rule. The activity suggested that an attacker, after obtaining access to the endpoint, executed PowerShell with the apparent objective  of preparing the system for subsequent malicious actions while minimizing traces of execution.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (Shortly after the initial execution, additional alerts indicated the creation of a Registry Run Key, establishing persistence on the compromised host. Further investigation revealed another alert showing that the same user account had been added to the local Administrators group, indicating a successful privilege escalation attempt. All three attack stages occurred within a very short timeframe, confirming a coordinated multi-stage attack.)
/E (Shortly after the initial execution, additional alerts indicated the creation of a Registry Run Key, establishing persistence on the compromised host. Further investigation revealed another alert showing that the same user account had been added to the local Administrators group, indicating a successful privilege escalation attempt. All three attack stages occurred within a very short timeframe, confirming a coordinated multi-stage attack.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (The investigation determined that the incident was limited to the Windows 10 Pro endpoint assigned to Amin, with no evidence of lateral movement to other systems. Immediate containment and remediation actions were performed to remove persistence, revoke the unauthorized administrative privileges, verify endpoint integrity, and restore the affected system to a secure operational state.)
/E (The investigation determined that the incident was limited to the Windows 10 Pro endpoint assigned to Amin, with no evidence of lateral movement to other systems. Immediate containment and remediation actions were performed to remove persistence, revoke the unauthorized administrative privileges, verify endpoint integrity, and restore the affected system to a secure operational state.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
